UNLICENSED — all rights reserved.

This is a placeholder and it is a real gap. A repository with no licence grants
nobody any rights, including collaborators, which is the correct default while
the question is open but is probably not what you want long term.

Pick one and replace this file:

  MIT         Do anything, keep the notice, no warranty. The usual choice for a
              personal project you might share.
  Apache-2.0  MIT plus an explicit patent grant and a requirement to state
              changes. Better if the project ever becomes serious.
  GPL-3.0     Anyone distributing a modified version must publish their source.
  Proprietary Keep this file as-is. Nobody may copy, modify or distribute it.

Whichever is chosen, it does NOT extend to the artwork assets in
src/renderer/assets/ — those belong to the artist. See docs/ARTWORK.md.

